WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.202
Really briefly, can you speak to rumors

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:04.004
that there is another Chinese balloon

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:04.971
above Alaska

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:06.139
or any other parts of the U.S.

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:08.708
territory that the U.S. shot down?

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:10.043
So I can confirm

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:11.544
that the Department of Defense

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:13.513
was tracking a high altitude object

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:14.114
over Alaska

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:17.484
airspace in the last 24 hours.

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:19.319
Out the

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:19.786
the object

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:22.255
was flying at an altitude of 40,000 feet

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:25.558
and posed a reasonable threat

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.794
to the safety of civilian flight

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.029
Out of an abundance of caution

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:30.430
and at the recommendation

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.798
of the Pentagon.

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:32.599
President Biden

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:34.634
ordered the military to down the object

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.603
and they did

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.004
and it came in inside

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:39.806
our territorial waters.

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.541
And those waters right now are frozen

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:42.809
but inside

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.677
territorial airspace

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.513
and over territorial waters.

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:48.815
Fighter aircraft assigned to U.S.

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:49.549
Northern Command

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.784
took down the object

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:53.019
within the last hour.

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:54.320
And we just go back for a moment.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.321
So

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.557
another aircraft of some sort,

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:59.325
airship balloon,

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:01.327
something was shot down today.

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.163
Who owns it?

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:05.532
What were the circumstances?

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:06.800
Was the president directly

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.401
involved in ordering this?

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.538
And is wreckage being recovered?

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.541
Well, Kate, so I'm going to try.

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:16.109
Remind me if I forget something.

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:16.409
Yes.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.010
The president

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.012
absolutely was involved in this decision.

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:20.580
He ordered it

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.247
at the

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.850
recommendation of Pentagon leaders.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.518
He wanted it taken down.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:26.786
And they did that.

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:28.288
They did it using fighter aircraft

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:30.090
assigned to U.S. Northern Command.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.291
The Pentagon will have more to say

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.326
about the details of this later

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:34.294
on this afternoon.

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:37.163
It's only just within the last hour

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:38.965
we're calling this an object

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.500
because that's the best description

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.135
we have right now.

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:44.938
We do not know who owns it,

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:46.172
whether it's a

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.174
whether it's state owned or

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.410
or corporate owned or privately owned.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:51.845
We just don't know.

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:53.313
We don't we don't know.

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.280
As I said, state owned.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.482
We don't know if it's state owned.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:59.352
And we don't understand the full purpose.

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:01.321
We don't have any comment.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.355
We don't have any information

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.690
that would confirm

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:06.192
a stated purpose for this object.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:08.361
We do expect to be able to recover

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:12.098
the debris since it fell not only

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:14.100
within our territorial space,

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.602
but on what we

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:19.472
what we believe is its frozen water.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:23.109
So it a recovery effort will be made.

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:24.310
And

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:26.746
we're hopeful that it'll be successful.

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:28.114
And then we can learn a little bit

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:28.915
more about it

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:30.083
with its appearance,

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:31.951
like the Chinese aircraft

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:35.221
No, it was it was much, much smaller

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:36.890
than the spy balloon

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:39.425
that we took down last Saturday.

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:40.994
The way it was described to me,

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:44.264
it was roughly the size of a small car

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:46.366
as opposed to

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:47.534
a payload

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:49.869
that was like two or three busses size.

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:51.571
Right. So much, much smaller.

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:56.042
And and they're not of the same.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.645
Not not no.

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:01.581
No significant payload if you will.

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:02.949
And lastly,

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:03.483
is it

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:05.952
now the policy of the United States

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:06.286
that if

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:08.521
